{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWh8bzWziQjsNncxPHiZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BtznsTdf26dUAiL8cjZAeM","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"interpretation":"The specification contribution chosen last time has run (result 7f26f5a0…). It wrote only specification/project-conformance.md. The current worksite observation a1afa1ea… shows that file present at sha256 a74a75b6… (25127 bytes), matching the reported digest.\n\nAccording to its author's report, the file contains:\n- the Intent and Product boundary;\n- authority order;\n- traversal of all eight original stages;\n- requirements REQ-01..REQ-14;\n- acceptance criteria AC-01..AC-15;\n- evidence lineage;\n- visible conflicts C1..C8;\n- unknowns U1..U5.\n\nThat report is an attributed observation, not an adequacy judgment. The conformance obligation stays open until independent assessment.\n\nThe corrected CLI (fe8f4080…) and the admitted C2 measurement b609386b… are unchanged and current. That measurement shows command 0 exiting 0 with exactly \"Hello, world!\\n\", and command 1 exiting 0 with 2 passes and 0 failures. All of its selected paths are still current, and writing the conformance asset did not touch any of them, so no new testing run is needed.\n\nThe revision lineage is intact:\n1. Baseline failure b63cfd1d… on the old bytes 647697a5…. It stays historical.\n2. Correction 50dd6daf….\n3. Fresh measurement b609386b… on the current bytes.\n\nThree authored assets are still absent: design/implementation-design.md, design/test-design.md and test-execution-plan.json. They have to be written against the actual conformance asset. That includes its C4 conflict (one plan command versus the two fixed commands), which the specification author explicitly deferred to the plan author, and C5 (assertedReturnValue without a newline versus stdout with one).\n\nAll seven obligations remain open. Parent completion also needs an independent assessment and agreement between the installed Public result and a replay. Only the parent can supply that agreement, and it is not claimed here.","contributions":[{"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/design@5","contribution":"Write three files from scratch, and only these. Use the actual current specification/project-conformance.md (sha256 a74a75b6…) as authority, and cite its REQ/AC identifiers where they apply (for example REQ-08..REQ-10 and AC-09..AC-11).\n\n(1) design/implementation-design.md\n- Defines the minimal Node CLI at generated/hello-world.mjs. It prints exactly \"Hello, world!\" plus one newline through a single console.log, with no imports, packages or network use, and runs under node without installation. This matches the current file fe8f4080….\n- Names test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs and test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs as the verification surfaces that execute the CLI and assert stdout.\n- States how the design traces back to the conformance requirements.\n\n(2) design/test-design.md\n- Specifies the component check 'CLI process satisfies its output contract' and the UAT check 'a user receives the exact promised greeting'.\n- Each check uses node:test, node:assert/strict and spawnSync to run process.execPath with [\"generated/hello-world.mjs\"] from the project root, and asserts status 0 and stdout exactly \"Hello, world!\\n\". This matches the actual supplied test bytes.\n- States the coverage floor: both files run, at least 2 passes and 0 failures.\n- Acknowledges the conformance unknowns that remain untested, such as arguments, stdin and stderr.\n\n(3) test-execution-plan.json\n- Top-level fields:\n  - command \"node\";\n  - args [\"--test\",\"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\",\"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\"];\n  - expectedTestPassCount of at least 2;\n  - expectedStdoutMatch containing the stable zero-failure fragment \"fail 0\", with no exact pass count pinned;\n  - assertedReturnValue exactly \"Hello, world!\".\n- Resolve conformance conflict C4 explicitly. The required top-level fields must stay intact. The plan may also declare the fixed direct CLI command `node generated/hello-world.mjs`, with expected stdout \"Hello, world!\\n\" and exit 0, as agreement data.\n- Resolve C5 explicitly: assertedReturnValue is the greeting text, and the stdout expectation carries the single trailing newline.\n- The plan states criteria only. It must not claim observed results or control execution.\n- No test-execution-result.json may be written. Execution-result meaning comes from the admitted C2 evidence plus independent assessment.","reason":"All three assets are absent and need substantive new content. The conformance asset they must follow now exists as admitted native work (7f26f5a0…). Its author deferred C4 and C5 to the plan and design owners, so this row carries those decisions. The admitted measurements b63cfd1d… and b609386b… show that the supplied verifiers really spawn the CLI, and that \"fail 0\" appears in actual passing output.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/implementation-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/test-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/execution-plan@5","obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5"],"evidenceRefs":["task://default-library-witness/s6-original@5","worksite-context-observation://abiogenesis/a1afa1eacd540c48a0cd5e7ceeae9801bbc0e70650bc572ec1e3153c958f5f76","result://abiogenesis/7f26f5a0fa42da01286419f23462cd02fee4cd275eb5e48cc316ed8cef34ea1e","result://abiogenesis/b609386b5e8027ffe1e90f95657472fde395a9fdc36c9dcfeccd01825659b470","result://abiogenesis/b63cfd1dc0bc193ebab9987177c88119d945add00bc62eaf4b955388dc513aea"],"dependsOn":[]},{"graphFunctionRef":"graph-function://abiogenesis/default-library/uat@5","contribution":"Carry out a read-only, independent assessment of the complete original outcome. The selected subject is the current C2 measurement b609386b…. The assessment reads:\n- the exact current candidate generated/hello-world.mjs (fe8f4080…);\n- the original source;\n- the oracle rubric;\n- the witness contract;\n- the four authored assets as they actually exist in the worksite.\n\nIt must cover:\n- the substantive content of specification/project-conformance.md (a74a75b6…) and how it corresponds to the source. This includes whether its conflict and unknown dispositions C1..C8 and U1..U5 are faithful, and whether the frame dispositions it proposed as non-material hold.\n- Whether the implementation design and test design follow the conformance asset and the actual supplied verifiers.\n- Whether the supplied verifiers are adequate: both really spawn the CLI and assert exit 0 and exact stdout.\n- Whether the plan agrees with the two fixed commands and the original expectations: at least 2 passes, 'fail 0', and assertedReturnValue \"Hello, world!\". Judge the C4 and C5 resolutions.\n- The current CLI's stdout and exit status, and the observed test counts.\n- The revision chain: baseline b63cfd1d… on 647697a5…, then correction 50dd6daf…, then measurement b609386b…. The measurement lists no producer pointer, so judge the causal link from lineage and digests. Also judge the sandbox-copy currentness relation (C7). Keep the baseline historical.\n\nKeep unmet and indeterminate criteria.","reason":"Parent completion requires an independent semantic assessment of the current admitted evidence across all seven obligations. The assessor must be distinct from every author and from the measurement producer. The authored-content criteria cannot be assessed until design produces the three remaining assets.","supportRefs":["obligation://default-library-witness/complete-original@5","obligation://default-library-witness/conformance@5","obligation://default-library-witness/implementation-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/test-design@5","obligation://default-library-witness/execution-plan@5","obligation://default-library-witness/behavior@5"